{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-delta-discipline", "file": "references/template-stamp-marker-separation.md", "content": "# Separating markers from a stamp template

For a grid with scattered single-color marks and a distinctive multicolor shape, map the output delta against the input before deciding the shape's role. Record each copied footprint's exact coordinates and colors, then compare those to both scattered markers and any instance embedded in the source template. The template's own center may or may not be an active marker; infer this from the demo, rather than assuming all similar-colored cells are equivalent.

Define one explicit anchor and offsets for every template cell, including vertical/asymmetric parts. Enumerate marker positions from the original input before applying any edits. Replay on each demo and compare the full output, including unchanged cells, overlap, clipping, and whether the source template persists. A visually plausible generic cross is not a substitute for the observed exact template.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-2/play/users/u093/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-delta-discipline/references/template-stamp-marker-separation.md"}
